WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.134
In this last lesson,

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:07.328
you will learn to adjust Zonal to your
hands and your habits, in Settings.

00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:09.252
The defaults suit most people.

00:00:09.252 --> 00:00:12.873
A few settings make a big difference if
your work is a bit different.

00:00:14.224 --> 00:00:19.292
Click the Zonal icon in the menu bar, and
choose Settings. The General tab opens.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:24.580
The activation key is the key you hold
while you drag. It is Shift by default.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.153
You can choose Option or Command instead.

00:00:27.548 --> 00:00:31.372
Pick another key if an app you use already
gives Shift-drag a meaning,

00:00:31.372 --> 00:00:32.409
like a design tool.

00:00:32.846 --> 00:00:36.794
Turn on Always show Zones if nearly every
drag ends in a Snap.

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:38.959
The Zones then show on every drag,

00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:42.652
and you hold the key only for a drag that
should not Snap.

00:00:43.456 --> 00:00:47.816
With a mouse that has side buttons, choose
the Back or Forward button here.

00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:51.189
Holding it shows the Zones, so you can
Snap with one hand.

00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:54.738
Zone picker turns the green button picker
on or off.

00:00:54.738 --> 00:00:58.486
Resize neighbouring windows together
controls the Shared edge.

00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:02.756
If you see the macOS tile preview flash
during your drags,

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:05.827
turn on Turn off macOS tiling while Zonal
runs.

00:01:05.827 --> 00:01:08.701
Zonal puts your settings back when it
quits.

00:01:09.491 --> 00:01:14.226
And if your keyboard says Ctrl, Alt and
Win, show key names instead of symbols.

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:16.897
Three examples.

00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:22.709
A designer whose design tool already uses
Shift-drag sets the activation key to

00:01:22.709 --> 00:01:23.193
Option.

00:01:23.193 --> 00:01:25.475
Both tools now work side by side.

00:01:25.825 --> 00:01:29.157
Someone who Snaps all day turns on Always
show Zones,

00:01:29.157 --> 00:01:32.048
and holds the key only for the rare free
drag.

00:01:32.398 --> 00:01:35.137
Someone with a gaming mouse uses a side
button,

00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:38.109
and arranges windows without touching the
keyboard.

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:40.230
To recap.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.211
Choose the activation key that suits your
apps,

00:01:43.211 --> 00:01:46.637
show the Zones on every drag if you Snap
all the time,

00:01:46.637 --> 00:01:49.428
and use a side button to Snap with one
hand.

00:01:49.428 --> 00:01:52.282
You'll find all of this in Settings,
General.

00:01:53.832 --> 00:01:55.506
That's the end of this series.

00:01:55.506 --> 00:01:59.748
You'll find every lesson, and much more,
in the Zonal guide. Happy Snapping.
